    "updated_at": "2022-11-16T17:07:40Z",
    "body": "No, an alternate regex is needed for -Xinternalversion\r\n\r\n-Xinternalversion on my system prints this for Java 19:\r\n\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (19.0.1+10) for bsd-amd64 JRE (19.0.1+10) (Zulu19.30+11-CA), built on Sep 22 2022 11:30:59 by \"zulu_re\" with clang Apple LLVM 12.0.0 (clang-1200.0.32.29)\r\n\r\nthis for JDK 17:\r\n\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (17.0.5+8-LTS) for bsd-amd64 JRE (17.0.5+8-LTS) (Zulu17.38+21-CA), built on Oct  7 2022 06:03:12 by \"zulu_re\" with clang 4.2.1 Compatible Apple LLVM 11.0.0 (clang-1100.0.33.17)\r\n\r\nor this for Java 8:\r\n\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (25.352-b08) for bsd-amd64 JRE (Zulu 8.66.0.15-CA-macosx) (1.8.0_352-b08), built on Oct  9 2022 02:39:15 by \"zulu_re\" with gcc 4.2.1 Compatible Apple LLVM 11.0.0 (clang-1100.0.33.17)\r\n\r\nAs you can see the position of the correct number is not consistent, that was the basis for my suggesting to use \"-version\" which has more consistent output:\r\n\r\nJava 19:\r\n\r\nopenjdk version \"19.0.1\" 2022-10-18\r\nOpenJDK Runtime Environment Zulu19.30+11-CA (build 19.0.1+10)\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM Zulu19.30+11-CA (build 19.0.1+10, mixed mode, sharing) \r\n\r\nJava 17:\r\n\r\nopenjdk version \"17.0.5\" 2022-10-18 LTS\r\nOpenJDK Runtime Environment Zulu17.38+21-CA (build 17.0.5+8-LTS)\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM Zulu17.38+21-CA (build 17.0.5+8-LTS, mixed mode, sharing)\r\n\r\nJava 8:\r\n\r\nopenjdk version \"1.8.0_352\"\r\nOpenJDK Runtime Environment (Zulu 8.66.0.15-CA-macosx) (build 1.8.0_352-b08)\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (Zulu 8.66.0.15-CA-macosx) (build 25.352-b08, mixed mode)\r\n\r\nHowever, I do see that there is a significant performance hit. So I found the following regex that seems to work with -Xinternalversion:\r\n\r\n(?: JRE.*\\\\()([\\d.]+)\r\n\r\n",
